{"id": "EUVD-2025-209298", "enisaUuid": "964c3ba8-5589-3da0-9693-7cf924e5ed8a", "description": "A container privilege escalation flaw was found in certain Ansible Automation Platform images. This issue arises from the /etc/passwd file being created with group-writable permissions during the build process. In certain conditions, an attacker who can execute commands within an affected container, even as a non-root user, can leverage their membership in the root group to modify the /etc/passwd file. This vulnerability allows an attacker to add a new user with any arbitrary UID, including UID 0, gaining full root privileges within the container.", "datePublished": "2026-04-08T13:55:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T17:10:12", "baseScore": 6.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:42141", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:42144", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:66482", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:66485", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:66486", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:66487", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:67279", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:71177", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:71179", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:71192", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:71210", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2025-57847", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2391092"], "aliases": ["GHSA-49g2-wpmf-55pv", "CVE-2025-57847"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0408f006-12a3-397f-b178-bfc04b431f89", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.7", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1789584820"}, {"id": "09bcc376-9cb0-399c-a4b1-8e223558e9f0", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.6", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patc